VERDICT: genuine incomplete fix confirmed at RUNTIME. Log4j 2.15.0 is NOT JNDI-safe: the
CVE-2021-44228 message-lookup-only fix is bypassed by carrying the SAME ${jndi:...} in
attacker-controlled MDC through a Context-Lookup pattern, and 2.15.0's own allowed-hosts list
lets the JNDI/LDAP connection to 127.0.0.1 resolve. Only 2.16.0 (remove message lookups + disable
JNDI) closes it.

